jimc@MATH.UCLA.EDU> writes:


> fetsi klupe (fetyklupe?) = female screw.  This male/female metaphor is
> standard, at least in electrical engineering.
> 
i'd broaden it to all engineering, including automotive engineering and 
carpentry, at least in english.  whether it's so in other languages i don't know.  

i just looked up the russian, which is "gajka - female screw, nut".  'female' 
there means 'enveloping, enclosing' (okhvatyvayushchij) or 'embracing, 
enveloping' (obnimayushchij).

so, at least in russian, the metaphor is lost.
